    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d177-a1">

                <pb facs="0422" n="298" xml:id="pg298"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 206.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">additional regulations for consular courts of the
                        united states of america in china</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-05-26"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 26,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In accordance with section 5 of the act of Congress approved June 22, 1860,
                    entitled “An act to carry into effect certain provisions in the treaties between
                    the United States, China, Japan, Siam, Persia, and other countries, giving
                    certain judicial powers to ministers and consuls, or other functionaries of the
                    United States in those countries, or for other purposes,” I, James B. Angell,
                    envoy extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary of the United States to the
                    Empire of China, do hereby decree the following regulations, which shall have
                    the force of law in the consular courts of China.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JAMES B. ANGELL.</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-06-02"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 2,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Assented to.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <signed>O. N. DENNY,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Consul-General</hi>.</signed>
                        <lb/>
                        <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                    >Ning-Po</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1881-06-04"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 4,
                            1881</date>.</dateline></closer>
                </postscript>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Assented to.</p>
                    <closer><signed>EDWARD C. LORD, <hi rendition="#italic">Consul</hi>.</signed>
                        <lb/>
                        <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                    >Ching-Kiang</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1881-06-08"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 8,
                            1881</date>.</dateline></closer>
                </postscript>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Assented to.</p>
                    <closer><signed>E. J. SMITHERS, <hi rendition="#italic">Consul</hi>.</signed>
                        <lb/>
                        <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                    >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1881-06-11"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 11,
                            1881</date>.</dateline></closer>
                </postscript>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Assented to.</p>
                    <closer><signed>ISAAC F. SHEPARD, <hi rendition="#italic">Consul</hi>.</signed>
                        <lb/>
                        <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                    >Foochow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1881-06-18"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 18,
                            1881</date>.</dateline></closer>
                </postscript>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Assented to.</p>
                    <closer><signed>J. C. A. WINGATE, <hi rendition="#italic">Consul</hi>.</signed>
                        <lb/>
                        <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                    >Amoy</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1881-06-23"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 23,
                            1881</date>.</dateline></closer>
                </postscript>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Assented to.</p>
                    <closer><signed>W. ELWELL GOLDSBOROUGH, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Consul</hi>.</signed>
                        <lb/>
                        <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                    >Swatow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1881-06-27"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 27,
                            1881</date>.</dateline></closer>
                </postscript>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Assented to.</p>
                    <closer><signed>C. C. WILLIAMS, <hi rendition="#italic">Consul</hi>.</signed>
                        <lb/>
                        <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                    >Canton, China</hi></placeName>.</dateline></closer>
                </postscript>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Assented to.</p>
                    <closer><signed>F. CARROW,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">United States Vice-Consul
                                in Charge</hi>.</signed>
                        <lb/>
                        <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                    >Tientsin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1881-07-20"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 20,
                            1881</date>.</dateline></closer>
                </postscript>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Assented to.</p>
                    <closer><signed>CHAS. L. FISHER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">United States
                                Vice-Consul in Charge</hi>.</signed>
                        <lb/>
                        <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                    >Newchwang</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1881-08-05"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 5,
                            1881</date>.</dateline></closer>
                </postscript>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Assented to.</p>
                    <closer><signed>J. J. FRED’K BANDINEL,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Vice-Consul</hi>.</signed></closer>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d177-a1-a1.xml" xpointer="d177-a1-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
